    "result_text": "The build is green. Let me summarize the change.\n\n## Summary\n\nMoved date-derived values to a fiscal-year basis (fiscal year starts **1 July**), driven off the business-day-adjusted `registrationDate`.\n\n**`Owner.java`** (`model/`):\n- Added `fiscalYearStart(LocalDate)` helper \u2014 returns the calendar year in which the fiscal year containing a date began (July\u2013Dec \u2192 same year; Jan\u2013Jun \u2192 previous year).\n- Added derived `getFiscalYear()` returning `FY<YY>` (e.g. a 2026-08-11 registration \u2192 `FY26`).\n- `getMembershipNumber()` now uses the **fiscal year's** last two digits for the `-M<YY>` segment instead of the calendar year.\n- `getMembershipPoints()` tenure now counts **elapsed fiscal years** (`fiscalYearStart(today) - fiscalYearStart(reg) > 1`) rather than a 365-day window.\n\n**`openapi.yml`**: added the read-only `fiscalYear` property (`^FY[0-9]{2}$`) to the `Owner` schema and updated the `membershipNumber`/`membershipPoints` descriptions to match. MapStruct auto-maps `fiscalYear` since the `Owner` getter matches the generated DTO property.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**: updated the `toBusinessDay` javadoc to mention the fiscal-year derivations.\n\nThe suite passes (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`), and the audit log confirms correct output: `registrationDate=2026-08-11 membershipNumber=NSW-16E6609E-M26` (FY26).\n\nOne deliberate interpretation worth flagging: the spec pins the format (`FY<YY>`) and the 1 July start but not the labelling convention or the exact tenure threshold. I labelled the fiscal year by the calendar year it **begins** in, and translated the old \"tenure exceeds 365 days\" rule to \"more than one elapsed fiscal year.\" Only the `FY\\d{2}` regex is test-enforced; if your business convention labels FYs by their **ending** year, or wants tenure to award points at \u22651 elapsed fiscal year, those two lines are where to adjust.",
